└── synchronous HTTP client for polling REST endpoints
    ├── Candidates : requests, httpx
    ├── Used APIs  : Session, session.get, resp.raise_for_status, resp.json
    ├── Pitfalls   : requests.Session() vs httpx.Client(): slightly different constructor options and connection pooling defaults; Timeout semantics differ: 
    │   requests uses a single float or tuple, httpx.Timeout is a distinct object type with separate connect/read/write timeouts; Exception hierarchies differ:
    │   requests.exceptions.HTTPError vs httpx.HTTPStatusError, requests.ConnectionError vs httpx.ConnectError; httpx.Client must be explicitly used in sync 
    │   mode (not httpx.AsyncClient) to match this file's synchronous design
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file uses requests.Session() to perform synchronous GET requests, check status codes, and parse JSON bodies. httpx.Client() supports an equivalent 
        synchronous API (get, raise_for_status, json) and can be used as a drop-in replacement for this usage pattern without switching to async code.

